{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncfg=json.load(open('update23.json'))['interpretations'][0]   # current config account\ncfg=json.loads(json.dumps(cfg))\ncfg['executions']['fe822d82c6264158826e0303b4ce59b1']=[4,6,7,8,11,13,15,16,17,18]\n\n# extend the authority paragraph with the precondition and the repeat's evidence\nold_auth=\\\"A node whose tracked configuration is empty therefore does not merely fail to win an election: it never attempts to acquire authority, so it cannot be the source of a new leader even when the surviving members could form a quorum with it. \\\"\nnew_auth=(\\\"A node whose tracked configuration is empty therefore does not merely fail to win an election: it never attempts to acquire authority, so it cannot be the source of a new leader even when the surviving members could form a quorum with it. \\\"\n \\\"The precondition is visible in the same operand: the empty configuration appears when the caller's store reports a non-zero persisted commit index, because that index becomes lastApplied and pushes the scan above the log's configuration entry. \\\"\n \\\"The repeat of this experiment (receipt fe822d82c6264158826e0303b4ce59b1) makes the dependence explicit: there A's persisted commit index was 0, so restoreFromCommittedLogs left lastApplied at zero, the scan started at index 1, A recovered the three-voter configuration (event 15: latest_config_index 1 with three members despite the replay being enabled) and it did attempt candidacy - 255 candidate samples in 267 (event 16), which is why the comparison for that execution returned unknown rather than a witness. The same repeat reproduced the other three cases with identical operands: the commit-rule case again tracked the snapshot's three-voter configuration against a log whose configuration entry has two voters and again committed with only the removed server's acknowledgement (events 2, 3, 4), the durable-snapshot case again recorded an empty configuration at index 0 in the snapshot metadata and again came up empty after a flag-off restart (events 6, 7, 8), and the availability case again committed with two members live and lost the ability after the second stop (events 11 and 13). \\\")\nassert old_auth in cfg['rationale']\ncfg['rationale']=cfg['rationale'].replace(old_auth,new_auth)\ncfg['rationale']=(\\\"Extension note: this successor reports the repeat of the multi-node experiment (receipt fe822d82c6264158826e0303b4ce59b1), which reproduced the commit-rule, durable-snapshot and availability cases with identical operands but not the authority witness, because the caller's persisted commit index was zero in that execution and the startup scan therefore recovered the configuration; the authority paragraph now states that precondition and the counterevidence records it. A revised experiment that holds the precondition explicitly has been submitted with this batch. \\\")+cfg['rationale']\n\ncfg['counterevidence'].append(\\\"The authority witness depends on a property of the caller's store: A's persisted commit index must be non-zero, because that value becomes lastApplied and pushes the startup scan above the log's configuration entry. The repeat of the experiment shows the other side of that condition - with a persisted commit index of 0 the scan starts at index 1, A recovers its configuration and does attempt candidacy (receipt fe822d82c6264158826e0303b4ce59b1, events 15 and 16). The receipt therefore bounds the claim to restarts whose store reports a non-zero commit index, which the original receipt's operand (staged commit index 4) shows for its own execution.\\\")\ncfg['limitations'].append(\\\"The authority witness has one execution in which its premise held and one repeat in which it did not, so it is currently a single valid witness; a revised version of the experiment that keeps committing until A's persisted commit index is non-zero has been submitted to make the premise deterministic, and its receipt is not yet part of this account.\\\")\ncfg['joint_history']+=\\\" Receipt fe822d82c6264158826e0303b4ce59b1 is the same fixed experiment as receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332 executed a second time in a fresh clean copy, which is why its events carry the same names and indices; the authority case is where the two differ, and the difference is the operand staged_commit_index (4 in the first execution, 0 in the repeat).\\\"\nout={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Reports the repeat of the multi-node experiment honestly (three cases reproduced identically, the authority witness did not because its precondition failed), states that precondition in the authority paragraph, and submits the revised experiment with a deterministic premise.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[cfg],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"98ee8dfd5fac4b84915f91ed4b094bcf-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"7db8c9fb0d794b08892b9349c54fa466-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"The repeat showed that the authority case's premise is not guaranteed: A's persisted commit index can be zero at restart, in which case the startup scan recovers the configuration and the witness conditions do not arise. The revised harness keeps committing through the leader until A's store reports a non-zero commit index before restarting A, and reports how many extra applies that took.\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_multi_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_newraft_startup\\\",\\\"src_restore_committed\\\",\\\"src_follower_election_guard\\\",\\\"src_process_config_entry\\\",\\\"src_quorum_size\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Same four cases as the predecessor harness, with one change: before A is restarted in the authority case, the harness commits further commands through the leader until A's commit-tracking store reports a non-zero persisted commit index, then restarts A and samples its state as before. The command count of that premise loop is reported as premise_filler_applies.\\\",\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"A's persisted commit index is what restoreFromCommittedLogs reads at startup; it advances when A's log store stages a write, so driving more leader commits makes it non-zero.\\\",\\\"The premise loop is bounded and the case fails loudly if twenty further applies do not make the value non-zero.\\\",\\\"Everything else about the authority case is unchanged: A restarts over its own stores with the case's replay setting, then the other voters are shut down and A's state is sampled every 5ms for 1500ms.\\\"],\\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No change to the other three cases in the harness.\\\",\\\"No assertion about winning an election; the observation remains the candidate attempt itself.\\\"],\\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"cases\\\":[\\\"empty_config\\\",\\\"recovered_config\\\"],\\\"premise_loop_cap\\\":20,\\\"sampling_interval_ms\\\":5,\\\"sampling_window_ms\\\":1500}},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"For each case the harness builds three assuranceMultiNode values, wires them, bootstraps the three-voter configuration and starts each node with a fresh MockFSM. It commits three commands through the elected leader, then keeps committing until A's commit-tracking store reports a non-zero commit index (at most twenty further applies, reported as premise_filler_applies), records that index, and shuts A down. A new transport on A's address is connected to B and C, NewRaft is called on A's stores with a fresh MockFSM and the case's replay setting, and the harness reports A's tracked configuration. B and C are then shut down and A's state is sampled every 5ms for 1500ms, reporting follower, candidate and leader sample counts, whether candidacy was attempted and the final state.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"raft's startup recovery is responsible for establishing the configuration the log already contains, and whether it does so depends on the persisted commit index the caller's log store reports, which the harness now establishes explicitly before testing the voter's ability to attempt authority.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_empty_config\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance.authority.restart.empty_config\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"value\\\":true},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"latest_config_voters\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]},{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_recovered_config\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance.authority.restart.recovered_config\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"value\\\":false},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"latest_config_voters\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}]}],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[{\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance.authority.attempt.empty_config\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_empty_config\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"attempted_candidacy\\\",\\\"value\\\":true},\\\"description\\\":\\\"With the premise held explicitly - a non-zero persisted commit index at A's restart - a voter whose log establishes the configuration must still attempt candidacy once the other voters are gone.\\\"},{\\\"event\\\":\\\"assurance.authority.attempt.recovered_config\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"case\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_recovered_config\\\",\\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"attempted_candidacy\\\",\\\"value\\\":true},\\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same node with the same log restarted with the replay disabled recovers its configuration and attempts candidacy.\\\"}]\n }\n}\njson.dump(out,open('update27.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('execs',len(cfg['executions']),'ce',len(cfg['counterevidence']),'lim',len(cfg['limitations']))\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update27.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\nimport sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('valid',d['valid'],'no_change',d.get('no_change'),'exec',d.get('execution_requested'))\nfor x in d.get('diagnostics',[])[:8]: print(x['paths'],x['message'])\nprint([(e['object'],e['action']) for e in d.get('effects',[])])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
